WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.200
More than a year after HBO's Westworld ended
its sophomore season, creators Jonathan Nolan

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.060
and Lisa Joy are finally taking the show to
a place fans have been waiting to see since

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.480
the beginning: the real world.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.860
Although Nolan has hinted that season 3 will
be, quote, "less of a guessing game," that

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.490
doesn't mean the show will be any less filled
with intriguing Easter eggs for sharp-eyed

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.040
fans.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.000
Obviously, spoilers for all of Westworld abound.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.400
Westworld takes great care with its use of
language.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.119
Character names often carry a deeper meaning
both Teddy Flood and Hector Escaton's surnames

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:34.110
have ties to the end of the world, while Ford
and Bernard are names that both appear in

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:38.170
Aldous Huxley's dystopian novel Brave New
World: Ford being Henry Ford, and, in the

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.239
novel, another word for God, while Bernard
is an alpha male resentful of his inability

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.320
to fit into society.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.340
Likewise, episode titles often point to something
deeper, like season 1's "Contrapasso," which

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:52.050
is a reference to the punishment of souls
in Dante's Inferno.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.859
Westworld's third season puts another biblical
reference front and center in the premiere

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.440
episode's title: "Parce Domine."

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.320
It's a Roman Catholic antiphon, or chant,
and it comes from the Book of Joel.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.620
The translation reads:

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.240
"Spare, Lord, spare your people: lest you
be angry with us forever."

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.439
It's commonly heard during the Lent season
the time in which Christians fast and forgo

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:14.939
physical pleasures as a means of recognizing
Christ's 40-day journey into the desert.

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:19.149
For Westworld, the significance is two-fold:
it could be representative of Dolores' long

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:23.220
journey into the real world, as she has already
set herself up as the Hosts' savior.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.670
It's also a call to be spared from a holy
wrath, to be granted mercy something Dolores

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.260
likely won't deliver.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:29.760
After all:

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.640
"The real gods are coming.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.660
And they're very angry."

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.240
When we first meet Caleb, it's as he wakes
up to begin his day.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.140
Much of what we see of Caleb is routine he
goes through the motions of his life, almost

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.260
as if he's on a loop.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.659
It doesn't take much to recognize the similarities
between Caleb and the host Maeve we met in

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.400
season 1.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:55.670
Just as Maeve did in Westworld's first season,
it's a pretty safe bet that Caleb will wind

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.100
up "waking up" from his reality in the coming
weeks.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.840
"Do you need some help?"

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.800
But Caleb isn't the only Westworld character
following a familiar path.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.160
By the end of the episode, Dolores has successfully
replaced Martin Connells, the head of security

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.480
for Incite, with a Host under her control.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.540
Incite, of course, is the data company that
controls The System, a thing Dolores would

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.020
very much like access to.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.500
So now Dolores has a Host posing as a high
ranking Delos board member, along with one

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.040
who works high level security.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.060
If we buy into the theory that Stubbs was
an undercover Host within the Westworld theme

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.530
park, then it's looking like Dolores is working
her own Ford magic in the real world, with

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.780
her own Arnold/Bernard and Stubbs stand-ins.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.620
What's become of Bernard since he made his
way back to the real world and had that ominous

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.040
first meeting with Dolores?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.000
Turns out, he isn't doing so well.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:52.120
Having gone into hiding following the Westworld
massacre, Bernard has been spending the last

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:54.100
few months living and working on a meat farm.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.590
The slaughtering of animals is work he has
some trouble with, but he makes do at least

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.790
until he's confronted by a couple of co-workers
and is forced to switch personalities in order

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.000
to handle the situation.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:08.460
Bernard, it seems, is able to switch between
personalities at the touch of a button or,

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:12.659
more accurately, he can alternate between
his character and analysis modes, which have

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.780
evolved into distinct personalities.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.120
It looks like much of his arc this season
will be in trying to put himself back together,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.930
and if you need hard evidence, you don't have
to look any further than the name he's using

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:22.840
as an alias.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.800
It's an anagram for "Damaged Arnold."

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.540
While it isn't necessarily a Grand Theft Auto
Easter egg, RICO, the app Caleb uses to make

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.500
money in his downtime, does certainly feel
like a nod to the famous video game.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:39.080
With tons of quick buck options and messages
like "You made bank, now get drank," it definitely

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.740
evokes a GTA vibe.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.180
This wouldn't be the first time the series
has been compared to the game, either.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.540
During its first season, Deadline likened
Westworld to being, quote, "more Grand Theft

00:03:48.549 --> 00:03:50.500
Auto than the Emmy-winning [Game of Thrones]."

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.430
In fact, Jonathan Nolan even cited the game
as a reference at the 2016 New York Comic-Con,

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:55.980
saying:

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:00.200
"We played some as research for making this
show, as when (Michael) Crichton first wrote

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.380
his movie, video games literally didn't exist
except for PONG.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.380
I'm happy to report my wife is the world's
most boring Grand Theft Auto player."

